ut it's clear that the protesters want  to keep the pressure up they want to be  on the streets and the law has clearly  not achieved what it should achieve  according to the government to deter the  protesters and take some steam out of  the situation no now the protesters are  more furious than ever and everybody is  where almost everybody is wearing a face  mask now to the demonstration even those  that were not wearing any before but  Matthias we now have the police actually  arresting demonstrators two of them have  now appeared in court for wearing face  masks can we really expect that the  protesters will continue to defy the ban  on face masks  it's hard to say at the moment it looks  like this and if you look at what has  happening throughout these four months  then that's that every means of  deterrence be it troops at the border  with China threatening to enter the city  be it police tactics that target the  protesters at an early stage all this  has not worked so far the people are not  deterred and that might be because many  protesters fear that if they stop to  protest a much worse clamp down on the  city will happen and Beijing will take  its revenge so so far of course the  things are very volatile and and and can  take other turns but at the moment it  doesn't look like this is going to deter  the protesters they were not deterred by  long terms for rioting people were  charged with offenses that carry up to  ten years in prison so one year in  prison for wearing a mask will probably  not do the job either  I understand public transport in Hong  Kong has been severely disrupted Matias  how is that impacting daily life there  yeah you can see here this is one of the  major MTR stations one of the most busy  MTR stations in Hong Kong it has been  vandalized for several days in a row  half of the transport system is down  today again even more than half and of  course this makes life here very  difficult to transport system carries  five million passengers a day today is a  public holiday so people are not most  people are not commuting to their jobs  that is of course changing tomorrow when  schools and most businesses will pick up  again and we will see how this is going  to work of the city is built on this  transport system and it needs it adheres  thank you very much Matthias Berliner  there in Hong Kong
 

